{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_133336_b90749", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_2ab5a185aa3248cfba97919a75766152 and the versioned RefSeq evidence. These qualifications are already incorporated in LABBOOK and the published synthesis.\n\nThe conclusion remains: QKI depletion alters reported PMP22 variant abundance, but the specific promoter, splicing or stability mechanism is unresolved pending primer/junction mapping. NM_000304.4 and NM_153321.3 differ in their 5′ UTRs and encode the same protein isoform; that does not establish what the paper’s assays measured. K562 shared-3′-UTR binding remains separate from the Schwann-precursor response.\n\nNo change to candidate ranking or published conclusions is needed. QKI is not claimed as a novel PMP22 connection. No new collection, rerun or courtesy follow-up was initiated.", "tokens": {"input": 10429, "output": 953, "total": 869878, "cache_read": 858496, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 44657, "timestamp": 1791246264014}
